   "id": "e44a535d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **Makemore**\n",
    "Makes more of things that you give it.\n",
    "- Character-level Language Model\n",
    "- Treats each line as an example: Treats each examples as a sequence of individual characters\n",
    "- Modeling sequence of characters \n",
    "- Predicting the next character in the sequence given an already concrete sequence of characters before it"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1758c9f2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "['emma', 'olivia', 'ava', 'isabella', 'sophia', 'charlotte', 'mia', 'amelia', 'harper', 'evelyn']\n",
      "32033\n",
      "2\n",
      "15\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "words = open('names.txt', 'r').read().splitlines() # reads file as single massive string --> splits string into list of words\n",
    "\n",
    "# quick inspection tool: allows to verify that file has loaded successfully\n",
    "print(words[:10]) # extracts & displays only first 10 in list\n",
    "\n",
    "print(len(words))\n",
    "# goes through each word in list to find min. and max. length of words in list\n",
    "print(min(len(word) for word in words))\n",
    "print(max(len(word) for word in words))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62d27cd4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## **Bigrams in Dataset**\n",
    "Sequence of two adjacent elements"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "53fcaaff",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "['e', 'm', 'm', 'a']"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 8,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# converts the String into individual character list\n",
    "list(w) "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "659a7c56",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "b = {} # initializes empty dictionary to store every unique bigram tuple (as key) and its frequency (as value)\n",
    "\n",
    "for w in words: # iterates up until indicated # word in list\n",
    "    # adds start and end tokens to each word in list\n",
    "    # without this, the model would not know when to start or stop generating a word\n",
    "    chs = ['<S>'] + list(w) + ['<E>'] \n",
    "\n",
    "    # zip(): pairs elements with matching indexes from OG and modified lift\n",
    "    # assigns ch1 and ch2 to corresponding word (index) in each list\n",
    "    for ch1, ch2 in zip(chs, chs[1:]):\n",
    "        bigram = (ch1, ch2) # creates tuple of each bigram (pair of characters)\n",
    "        b[bigram] = b.get(bigram, 0) + 1 # adds bigram to dictionary and increments its frequency by 1\n",
    "        print(ch1, ch2) "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "a3417d4f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "[(('q', 'r'), 1),\n",
       " (('d', 'z'), 1),\n",
       " (('p', 'j'), 1),\n",
       " (('q', 'l'), 1),\n"
       ...
       " (('<S>', 'a'), 4410),\n",
       " (('a', 'n'), 5438),\n",
       " (('a', '<E>'), 6640),\n",
       " (('n', '<E>'), 6763)]"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 17,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# takes sequence and rearranges it in ascending order based on the frequency of each bigram\n",
    "# kv[1] is the metric used by sorted() to determine the order of the bigrams in the dictionary\n",
    "sorted(b.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aae2d350",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## **Counting Bigrams in 2D Torch Tensor**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0f557061",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "id": "8e169f1d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "N = torch.zeros((28, 28), dtype=torch.int32) # initializes a 28x28 tensor of zeros to store the frequency of each bigram"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7ba511ea",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# combines names into one string, extracts unique characters, and sorts them in alphabetical order\n",
    "chars = sorted(list(set(''.join(words)))) \n",
    "# maps each char to a unique integer index\n",
    "stoi = {s:i for i,s in enumerate(chars)} # enumerate: allows loop while keeping track of postion index \n",
    "# adds start and end tokens to the dictionary of unique characters\n",
    "stoi['<S>'] = 26\n",
    "stoi['<E>'] = 27"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "id": "83bf0009",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "for w in words:\n",
    "    chs = ['<S>'] + list(w) + ['<E>'] \n",
    "    for ch1, ch2 in zip(chs, chs[1:]):\n",
    "        ix1 = stoi[ch1]\n",
    "        ix2 = stoi[ch2] \n",
    "        N[ix1, ix2] += 1\n"
   ]
  },
